1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,580
Exercise 1-54, shifting your voice position. You should feel a high vibration

2
00:00:07,580 --> 00:00:13,260
in your nasal passages as well as in your fingers. Now continue holding your nose

3
00:00:13,260 --> 00:00:19,700
and completely relax your throat. Allow an ah sound to flow from deep in your chest.

4
00:00:20,340 --> 00:00:26,220
Ah. There should be no vibration in your nose at all. Go back and forth several

5
00:00:26,220 --> 00:00:35,540
times. Ah, ah, ah, ah. Next, we practice flowing from one position to the other so

6
00:00:35,540 --> 00:00:41,060
you can feel exactly when it changes from a nasal sound to a deep, rich schwa.

7
00:00:41,520 --> 00:00:46,100
Remember how it was imitating a man's voice when you were little? Do that, pinch

8
00:00:46,100 --> 00:00:54,920
your nose, and repeat after me. Ah, ah, ah, ah. Here, we'll practice the same

9
00:00:54,920 --> 00:00:57,760
progression, sound.

10
00:01:00,880 --> 00:01:09,200
There are three nasal consonants, M, N, and NG. These have non-nasal counterparts,

11
00:01:09,680 --> 00:01:16,740
M and B, N and D, NG and G. We're going to practice totally denasalizing your voice

12
00:01:16,740 --> 00:01:21,740
for a moment, which means turning the nasals into the other consonants. We'll

13
00:01:21,740 --> 00:01:27,100
read the same sentence three times. The first will be quite nasal. The second will

14
00:01:27,100 --> 00:01:31,580
sound like you have a cold. The third will have appropriate nasal consonants but

15
00:01:31,580 --> 00:01:38,540
denasalized vowels. Repeat after me. Mary might need money. Mary might need money.

16
00:01:39,560 --> 00:01:40,820
Mary might need money.
